    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13617" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-virgĭno</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to deprive of
				virginity, to deflour</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., <i><span class="en">Petr. 25, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 1,
				18, 21</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juvenculam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Sirach, 20, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b> in the <i>pass.</i>,
			of young persons, <i>to quit the period of youth</i>,
			Varr. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 458, 26</span></i>.</div>
